A||N||10||trigger||general sunroof questions||||1||
Z||000000||trigger||06-20-2001||04:16 PM||||I have a few questions about factory sunroofs.  I know there is another topic started similar to this but mine are different questions.<P>-Where all of the factory sunroofs tinted, and what were the differences in the tint styles?<P>-Would a sunroof off of an 85 SE have the drain holes.<P>-Did all the sunroofs have black latches, even with tan interior?<P>-Did some sunroofs have diferent latch styles?  I know a guy in town has an 86 SE 4cyl/auto that has the factory sunroof.  He has to pull out about a 3 inch pin then lift out the sunroof.  I know a friend of mine has an 86 GT V-6/4 spd on his dealership that you just push two buttons on the latch, and then the sunroof lifts out.<P>-Did all sunroof cars have the same storage hardware under the hood?<P>-Will an 85 SE headliner work in my 88 coupe.<P>I think that's it for now.  Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Honestly officer, I was just keeping up with the flow of traffic.  I know there aren't any cars in the area, that's how far behind I am.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Trigger.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||06-20-2001||04:37 PM||||I'm pretty sure all of the sunroofs were tinted the same.  I've had two '85s (both GTs with A/C) and two '86s (1 base coupe w/o A/C and my current ride, a GT w/ A/C).  All of them have had sunroofs and all of them have been identical.<P>The sunroof itself doesn't have the drain holes, the frame does.  And, no.  The '85 won't have the drain holes, but that's easy to fix yourself.  Just drill a hole in each front corner (don't remember the size, but very small).<P>As far as I know, all of the sunroof hardware was black.  All have the same latch style.  Press two buttons to release.<P>All sunroof cars had the same storage hardware under the hood (assuming the sunroof was installed at the factory).<P>A headliner from an '85 SE will work as far as the sunroof is concerned but won't physically fit since the '85 didn't have the 3rd brake light and the '86s and up did.  You'll have to cut out the notch for the 3rd brake light, then probably recover your headliner.  (Not a difficult task assuming your headliner board is in decent shape.)<P>Hope I helped a little bit.<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000002||Galen||06-20-2001||05:02 PM||||I'll second him on the ease of drillin the holes. I drilled mine in like 5 minutes..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I took a long time cuz I was bored and had to find the stupid drill.<P>Every fiero I've seen with a sunroof(2) has had the same latching thingie..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/devil.gif">       <BR>   <A HREF="mailto:galen@spinrpg.com">galen@spinrpg.com</A>    -<A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>1988 Hawaiin Orchid Coupe w/ sunroof</A><BR>AIM: GalenRPG - <A HREF="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>WebJolt Pictures</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||06-20-2001||05:30 PM||||I understand that the 84s and the non-GT 85s just had tinted sunroof glass. GT 85s and all 86 and up had the "matrix" border around the edges of the glass.<BR>This from a friend who has parted out about 20 or so...<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||06-20-2001||07:23 PM||||I never paid much attention to the matrix thing.  I just noticed the matrix pattern on the sunroof in 4Play ('86 GT), but that came out of an '85 GT (which in turn--I think--came out of an '84----who knows where it started out?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> ).  I don't think the matrix pattern would make any noticable difference other than looks, would it? <P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000005||Songman||06-20-2001||07:46 PM||||And although they are the same style, the latch mechanism is different on 84s to 88s anyway. This coming from comparison of my Indy to the 88s that I have. I can't say of others.<P>They are all black and work the same way, but the 84 is a lot thinner, seemingly more cheaply made, than the 88.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||trigger||06-20-2001||11:14 PM||||Ok. Thanks for the info.  I saw all the posts on the drain holes, so I guess I'll have to drill some when I paint the roof.  I guess I'll also have to see the difference between the dot matrix tint, and the other.  Maybe I'll see if somebody wants to trade with me.  Thanks again.||||reg||1
